Good — the create_pr tests already set `AGENT: "engineer"`. So I can extend the "records the comment it ends the run on" test (id: 22) to assert the comment body carries the agent tag, but its fake `issue comment` response is a URL, not a body... The log carries the argv including `--body`. So I can find the `issue comment` call and read the body from the log.

Now let me write the tests.

Test A — turn-comment.test.ts:
```ts
  // #354: the run that parks on a child posts no result comment, so this ending is the
  // only footprint it leaves. Without the name on it, the aggregation that collects the
  // park had nobody to re-invoke.
  test("names the agent that ended the turn, when the caller knows it", () => {
    const body = turnCommentBody({ ended: "waiting", audience: "person", agent: "atomaton", body: "Launched: #7" });
    const lines = body.split("\n");
    expect(lines[0]).toBe(LLM_CONTEXT_TAG.write("exclude"));
    expect(lines[1]).toBe(AGENT_TAG.write("atomaton"));
    expect(lines[2]).toBe(ENDED_TAG.write({ verb: "waiting", answers: 0, run: 0 }));
    expect(mostRecentAgent([body])).toBe("atomaton");
  });

  test("writes no agent tag when the caller has no name, rather than an empty one", () => {
    const body = turnHeader({ ended: "waiting", audience: "person", agent: "  " });
    expect(body).toEqual([...]);  // exactly two lines
    expect(body.join("\n")).not.toContain(AGENT_TAG.marker);
  });
```

`AGENT_TAG.marker` is "atomaton:agent". Good.

Test B — tags.test.ts for isResultComment: a request-comment (with agent tag + ended done) counts; waiting does not; quotation does not; fenced sample does not.

Test C — mcp.test.ts launch_sub_agent: add AGENT: "atomaton" to the env and assert `mostRecentAgent([body])` → "atomaton". But careful: the existing test asserts `whooseTurn(events)` etc. I'll extend it. Need to import mostRecentAgent in mcp.test.ts — check imports.

Actually, is `mostRecentAgent` imported already in mcp.test.ts? Let me check. It uses `readers`, `turnEvents`, `whoseTurn`. I'll add the import from ../../../adapters/github/agent-on-issue.ts.

Test D — mcp.test.ts create_pr: in the "records the comment" test, look for the issue comment body and assert the agent tag. But that test's fake response for `issue comment` yields a URL (the postTurnComment returns an id) — the body is in the logged argv. Let me add a check after `recorded` assertion:

```ts
      const commented = readFileSync(log, "utf8").trim().split("\n").map((l) => JSON.parse(l) as string[])
        .find((argv) => argv[0] === "issue" && argv[1] === "comment");
